# HTTP headers for the almamesh.com Cloudflare Pages deployment.
# Vite copies this verbatim from public/ into dist/; Pages parses it (it is
# never served as an asset).
#
# Pages semantics (verified against `wrangler pages dev`, which runs the same
# asset-serving code as production — see docs/deploy/almamesh-com.md):
#   - EVERY matching rule applies; same-name headers MERGE into one comma-joined
#     value ("no-cache, public, max-age=…" — which browsers resolve as no-cache).
#     So each Cache-Control override below DETACHES the catch-all value first
#     with "! Cache-Control" before setting its own.
#
# DELIBERATELY NO COEP: the app runs NON-cross-origin-isolated by design
# (Pyodide module Workers + the embedding/worker behavior depend on it; the
# in-browser embedder even pins numThreads=1 for non-isolated hosts).
# Cross-origin isolation requires COOP:same-origin *AND* COEP:require-corp
# together — so `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy` is the one that must stay absent.
# COOP alone leaves `self.crossOriginIsolated === false` (asserted by the
# security-headers e2e), so it is set below: it puts this document in its own
# browsing-context group, severing `window.opener` from any cross-origin popup.
# DO NOT add Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy.

# --- Default: safe headers + revalidation + no edge body transforms. ----------
# Everything not overridden below rides this: index.html, the SPA-fallback HTML
# for client routes (/dashboard, /predictive, /mesh, …), sw.js, the
# manifest.webmanifest, version.json, build.json, public.key, /bundle/latest,
# icons.
# `no-transform` prevents Cloudflare Web Analytics (or another proxy feature)
# from injecting third-party scripts into the local-first application shell.
#
# --- connect-src is THE enforcement of the privacy claim ----------------------
# "Your data never leaves the device" has to be structurally true, not merely
# asserted. `connect-src` used to read `'self' https: http:`, which permits a
# fetch/XHR/WebSocket to ANY origin on the internet (cleartext included) — the
# header was present but measured nothing. It is now a CLOSED allowlist of the
# only destinations the shipped code can reach. Every entry is justified:
#
#   'self'                              every engine asset, /bundle/*, /models/*,
#                                       /pyodide/*, public.key, version.json and
#                                       the /api/feedback Pages Function.
#   https://openrouter.ai               opt-in BYO-key cloud LLM. The one-click
#                                       preset (packages/llm/src/config.ts
#                                       OPENROUTER_API_BASE) and normalizeKnownBase
#                                       force every openrouter.ai host to
#                                       https://openrouter.ai/api/v1.
#   https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com  city typeahead — the ONE declared,
#                                       owner-approved egress (see the README
#                                       network inventory and the header comment
#                                       in src/lib/geo/onlineGeocoder.ts). Only a
#                                       typed city string leaves; never birth data.
#   http://localhost:*  http://127.0.0.1:*
#                                       LOOPBACK ONLY = still on-device. Any port,
#                                       because a local OpenAI-compatible server is
#                                       Ollama (11434), LM Studio (1234) or
#                                       llama.cpp (8080) depending on the user.
#                                       Loopback is "potentially trustworthy" per
#                                       W3C secure-contexts, so upgrade-insecure-
#                                       requests does NOT rewrite it to https —
#                                       verified by the security-headers e2e.
#
# DELIBERATE BEHAVIOUR CHANGE, recorded so nobody "fixes" it by accident: a
# custom endpoint on a NON-loopback host — a LAN box (http://192.168.1.10:11434)
# or a third-party OpenAI-compatible proxy — is now blocked by this policy.
# `isLocalEndpoint` in packages/llm/src/config.ts still accepts RFC-1918 hosts
# (it mirrors the backend privacy gate), but CSP has no syntax for an IP range,
# and a private-network host genuinely does leave the device. If the owner wants
# a specific extra endpoint back, add THAT ONE ORIGIN here. Never restore bare
# `https:` / `http:` — that is the finding this file exists to close.
# The allowlist is pinned by src/lib/__tests__/securityHeaders.test.ts.
/*
  ! Access-Control-Allow-Origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://openrouter.ai https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com http://localhost:* http://127.0.0.1:*; frame-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; manifest-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), geolocation=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache, no-transform

# --- Immutable: content-hashed app shell (Rollup [name]-[hash] filenames) ----
/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Workbox runtime is emitted content-hashed at the root (workbox-<hash>.js).
/workbox-*.js
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# --- Immutable: engine data --------------------------------------------------
# Pyodide dist is version-pinned; the SW already CacheFirst-pins it for a year,
# so a long browser cache matches the design (a Pyodide bump ships as a new
# build + SW update, not as a changed URL).
/pyodide/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Signed bundle: chunk/ + manifest/ entries are content-addressed (sha256 file
# names) -> genuinely immutable. NOTE: /bundle/latest is NOT matched by these
# globs — it is the mutable update pointer and stays no-cache (rule below).
/bundle/chunk/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/bundle/chunks/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/bundle/manifest/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/bundle/manifests/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Self-hosted RAG model (MiniLM ONNX) + onnxruntime-web wasm: version-pinned,
# SW CacheFirst, fetched once on first chat use.
/models/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Self-hosted fonts (stable @fontsource snapshots, SW-precached).
/fonts/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Planet artwork: stable but NOT fingerprinted — cache a day so art swaps
# propagate without a URL change.
/planets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# --- Update signals: explicitly no-cache (redundant with /* today, but these
# gate the entire update flow — keep them pinned even if the catch-all changes).
/bundle/latest
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/sw.js
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/version.json
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/build.json
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/manifest.webmanifest
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/public.key
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache
